	(text "Vds < 100V\nIds < 120A\nQg ~ 150nC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.65 67.056 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.143 1.143)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4233c878-6fce-4830-9dc5-507fd1826b22")
	)
	(text "- Pair of FETs act as bidir switch,\n preventing flow in and out of solr\n leads when switched off.\n- 470K Res is path for gate discharge.\n- Bipolar Q enables MCU to actively\n switch off solr (rather than only\n reverse polarity events)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.206 119.126 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "860910db-2855-4c23-b96f-9e96d459dd35")
	)
	(text "Use constant current driver device because\nthe voltage on Pwr bus is not a constant.\n\nRext sets current in LED; According to DS:\n\"The current flowing into pin LED is\nproportional to the current flowing out\nof pin RS by a ratio of about 520:1\"\n\n30K sets current to ~20mA according to\ndatasheet graph (Infineon Fig3). For the\nAPT3216SRCPRV LED the current limit is\n(10mA .. 28mA).\n\nRext = (Iout / 610.53) ^ -1.005632\n\n[30K < Rext < 60K] results in [20mA < If 10mA]\nso something like 42..46K should be good.\n\nBCR430 Max supply voltage: 42V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.67 104.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ddc9378a-d67e-447b-a0a5-57b504a9bef8")
	)
